PVD("saudi_arabia_vision_2016-2030",{"docs":["","KSA Vision 2030"],"s":{"1":[[1,"6","1","Talent and Capacity Development Programme","we will expand and further develop our talents and capacity",""],[1,"6","2","Education and Training Opportunity Programme","providing opportunities for all through education and training",""],[1,"12","1","Market-Aligned Education System","building an education system aligned with market needs",""],[1,"27","4","Academic and Educational System Reform","We intend to embed positive moral beliefs in our children’s characters from an early age by reshaping our academic and educational system.",""],[1,"35","2","Early Childhood Education Development Investment","We will invest particularly in developing early childhood education",""],[1,"35","2","National Curriculum Refinement","refining our national curriculum",""],[1,"35","2","Teacher and Educational Leader Training","training our teachers and educational leaders",""],[1,"35","2","Vocational Training Expansion","We will also expand vocational training in order to drive forward economic development",""],[1,"35","2","Priority-Oriented International Scholarship Programme","Our scholarship opportunities will be steered towards prestigious international universities and be awarded in the fields that serve our national priorities",""],[1,"36","2","Lifelong Training and Workforce Performance Initiative","We will place a renewed emphasis on lifelong training and we will seek to make the most of the potential of our workforce by encouraging a culture of high performance.",""],[1,"39","2","Higher Education–Labour Market Alignment Reform","We will close the gap between the outputs of higher education and the requirements of the job market.",""],[1,"39","2","Student Career Guidance Programme","We will also help our students make careful career decisions",""],[1,"39","2","Student Training and Education Pathway Transition Support","training them and facilitating their transition between different educational pathways",""],[1,"39","3","Modern Curriculum Development Programme","We will prepare a modern curriculum focused on rigorous standards in literacy, numeracy, skills and character development.",""],[1,"39","3","Industry and Apprenticeship Skills Partnership Programme","We will invest in strategic partnerships with apprenticeship providers, new skills councils from industry, and large private companies.",""],[1,"39","3","Education Field Job Specification Development","We will also work towards developing the job specifications of every education field.",""],[1,"40","3","Centralized Student Database System","we will build a centralized student database tracking students from early childhood through to K-12 and beyond into tertiary education (higher and vocational) in order to improve education planning, monitoring, evaluation, and outcomes.",""],[1,"32","2","Irtiqaa School Parent Engagement Measurement Program","We will launch the “Irtiqaa” program, which will measure how effectively schools are engaging parents in their children’s education.",""],[1,"32","2","Parent-Led School Boards and Discussion Forums","We will establish parent-led boards in schools, to open discussion forums and further engage with parents.",""],[1,"32","2","Teacher Training for Parent Communication","Teachers will receive training to raise their awareness of the importance of communicating with parents and equip them with effective methods to do so successfully.",""],[1,"32","2","Cross-Sector Educational Partnership Programs and Events","We will also collaborate with private and non-profit sectors to offer innovative educational programs and events that can improve this academic partnership.",""],[1,"27","1","Family Support and Child Development Programme","we will provide our families with all the necessary support to take care of their children and develop their talents and abilities.",""],[1,"27","1","Parental Participation in Education","we want to deepen the participation of parents in the education process, to help them develop their children’s characters and talents so that they can contribute fully to society.",""],[1,"68","1","King Salman Program for Human Capital Development","KING SALMAN PROGRAM FOR HUMAN CAPITAL DEVELOPMENT",""]],"2":[[1,"28","1","Employment Preparation and Training Programme","Together with the private sector and non-governmental organizations, we will offer preparation and training to those unable to find employment so they can smoothly join the workforce whenever possible.",""],[1,"35","2","National Labor Gateway","We have launched the National Labor Gateway (TAQAT)",""],[1,"36","2","Job Creation and Anti-Unemployment Coordination Mechanism","These efforts will be coordinated by the recently established Job Creation and Anti-Unemployment Commission.",""],[1,"36","2","Youth Skills Development and Deployment Programme","We will guarantee their skills are developed and properly deployed.",""],[1,"36","2","Youth Entrepreneurship and Enterprise Expansion","by harnessing our youth’s energy and by expanding entrepreneurship and enterprise opportunities.",""],[1,"36","2","Women’s Talent and Productive Capability Development","we will continue to develop their talents, invest in their productive capabilities and enable them to strengthen their future and contribute to the development of our society and economy.",""],[1,"36","2","Disability-Inclusive Education and Employment Support","We will also enable those of our people with disabilities to receive the education and job opportunities that will ensure their independence and integration as effective members of society.",""],[1,"36","5","Diverse Job Opportunities Generation Policy","REINFORCE THE ABILITY OF OUR ECONOMY TO GENERATE DIVERSE JOB OPPORTUNITIES",""],[1,"36","5","Global Talent Attraction Paradigm","INSTITUTE A NEW PARADIGM IN ATTRACTING GLOBAL TALENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS.",""],[1,"72","3","Corporate Social Responsibility and Youth Career Opportunities Initiative","We will encourage the businesses that follow through on this commitment to participate in our country and to address national challenges.",""]],"3":[[1,"6","2","High-Quality Health Services","high quality services such as employment initiatives, health, housing, and entertainment",""],[1,"28","2","Hospital and Health Care Capacity Optimization","We are determined to optimize and better utilize the capacity of our hospitals and health care centers, and enhance the quality of our preventive and therapeutic health care services.",""],[1,"28","2","Preventive Health Care Promotion","The public sector will focus on promoting preventive care",""],[1,"28","2","Infectious Disease Reduction Initiative","The public sector will focus on ... reducing infectious diseases",""],[1,"28","2","Primary Care First-Contact Promotion","The public sector will focus on ... encouraging citizens to make use of primary care as a first step.",""],[1,"28","2","Health and Social Care Integration","It will deepen collaboration and integration between health and social care",""],[1,"28","2","Family-Supported Home Care","supporting families to provide home care when necessary for their relatives",""],[1,"28","2","Health Care Planning and Regulatory Oversight","The public sector will focus on its planning, regulatory and supervisory roles in health care.",""],[1,"28","2","Public Corporation Health Care Delivery","We intend to provide our health care through public corporations both to enhance its quality and to prepare for the benefits of privatization in the longer term.",""],[1,"28","2","Private Medical Insurance Development","We will work towards developing private medical insurance to improve access to medical services and reduce waiting times for appointments with specialists and consultants.",""],[1,"28","2","Doctor Training for Chronic Disease Treatment","Our doctors will be given better training to improve treatment for chronic diseases such as heart disease, diabetes and cancer that threaten our nation’s health.",""],[1,"32","3","Healthcare Corporatization Reform","CORPORATIZATION: EFFICIENT AND HIGH QUALITY HEALTH CARE",""],[1,"32","4","Healthcare Corporatization and Provider Competition Reform","To achieve this goal, we will introduce corporatization into the sector by transferring the responsibility for health care provision to a network of public companies that compete both against each other and against the private sector.",""]],"4":[[1,"6","2","Housing Services Provision","high quality services such as employment initiatives, health, housing, and entertainment",""],[1,"27","1","Housing Laws and Regulatory Reform","We will meet this target by introducing a number of laws and regulations;",""],[1,"27","1","Private-Sector Housing Construction Initiative","encouraging the private sector to build houses;",""],[1,"27","1","Housing Funding Mechanism","providing funding",""],[1,"27","1","Mortgage Solutions for Homeownership","mortgage solutions",""],[1,"27","1","Homeownership Schemes","ownership schemes that meet the needs of our citizens.",""],[1,"36","4","Non-Saudi Real Estate Ownership Policy","extending their ability to own real estate in certain areas",""]],"5":[[1,"16","2","Museum Establishment Programme","We will establish more museums",""],[1,"16","2","Tourist and Cultural Site Development","prepare new tourist and historical sites and cultural venues",""],[1,"16","4","National Identity Preservation and Promotion Initiative","We will endeavor to strengthen, preserve and highlight our national identity",""],[1,"16","4","Cultural Heritage Site Restoration Programme","We will continue to work on the restoration of national, Arab, Islamic and ancient cultural sites",""],[1,"16","4","International Registration of Cultural Heritage Sites","strive to have them registered internationally to make them accessible to everyone",""],[1,"16","4","Cultural Events Development Programme","create cultural events",""],[1,"16","4","World-Class Museum Development Initiative","build world-class museums",""],[1,"20","4","Islamic Museum and Research Center","We will build an Islamic museum in accordance with the highest global standards, equipped with the latest methods in collection, preservation, presentation and documentation.",""],[1,"43","2","Historical and Heritage Sites Development Programme","prepare and develop our historical and heritage sites",""]],"6":[[1,"6","2","Entertainment Services Development","high quality services such as employment initiatives, health, housing, and entertainment",""],[1,"21","2","Cultural and Entertainment Events Support Programme","We will support the efforts of regions, governorates, non-profit and private sectors to organize cultural events.",""],[1,"21","2","Cultural and Entertainment Investment Financing Mechanism","We intend to enhance the role of government funds, while also attracting local and international investors",""],[1,"21","2","International Entertainment Partnerships","creating partnerships with international entertainment corporations",""],[1,"21","2","Land Provision for Cultural and Entertainment Projects","Land suitable for cultural and entertainment projects will be provided",""],[1,"21","2","Creative Talent Support Programme","talented writers, authors and directors will be carefully supported",""],[1,"21","2","Cultural Venues and Entertainment Facilities Development","We will seek to offer a variety of cultural venues – such as libraries, arts and museums – as well as entertainment possibilities to suit tastes and preferences.",""],[1,"21","5","Sports Participation and Facilities Development Programme","We intend to encourage widespread and regular participation in sports and athletic activities, working in partnership with the private sector to establish additional dedicated facilities and programs.",""],[1,"26","2","DAEM Meaningful Entertainment Programme","“DAEM” MEANINGFUL ENTERTAINMENT FOR CITIZENS",""],[1,"26","3","Cultural and Entertainment Venues Development","We will increase the number and variety of cultural and entertainment activities with the aim of opening dedicated venues to showcase our citizens’ myriad talents.",""],[1,"26","3","Cultural and Social Clubs Regulatory Simplification","We will also review our regulations to simplify the establishment and registration of amateur, social and cultural clubs.",""],[1,"26","3","Daem Cultural Activities Support Programme","We will launch and provide the necessary financial support for “Daem”, a national program to enhance the quality of cultural activities and entertainment.",""],[1,"27","4","Cultural Social Volunteering and Athletic Activities Promotion","We will also promote cultural, social, volunteering and athletic activities through empowering our educational, cultural and entertainment institutions.",""]],"7":[[1,"6","1","Holy Sites Visitor Access Initiative","We will do our utmost to ensure that Muslims from around the world can visit the Holy Sites.",""],[1,"15","5","Third Expansion of the Two Holy Mosques","we have recently begun a third expansion to the Two Holy Mosques",""],[1,"15","5","Airport Modernization and Capacity Expansion","modernizing and increasing the capacities of our airports",""],[1,"15","5","Makkah Metro Project","We have launched the Makkah Metro project",""],[1,"15","5","Railroad and Train Projects for Holy Mosque Visitors","the railroad and train projects that will serve visitors to the Holy Mosques",""],[1,"16","2","Pilgrimage Experience Improvement Initiative","improve the pilgrimage experience within the Kingdom",""],[1,"20","2","Umrah Capacity and Service Quality Expansion","By increasing the capacity and by improving the quality of the services offered to Umrah visitors, we will, by 2020, make it possible for over 15 million Muslims per year to perform Umrah and be completely satisfied with their pilgrimage experience.",""],[1,"20","2","Automated Umrah Visa Application Reform","We will achieve this by improving visa application procedures which will smooth the visa process with the aim of full automation.",""],[1,"20","2","Pilgrim E-Services Integration","We will also further integrate e-services into the pilgrims’ journey, which will enrich the religious and cultural experience.",""],[1,"20","2","Pilgrim Accommodation Upgrading Initiative","Both the public and private sectors will play a crucial role in this project as we work to upgrade accommodation",""],[1,"20","2","Pilgrim Hospitality Improvement Initiative","Both the public and private sectors will play a crucial role in this project as we work to upgrade accommodation, improve hospitality and launch new services for pilgrims.",""],[1,"20","2","New Pilgrim Services Launch","Both the public and private sectors will play a crucial role in this project as we work to upgrade accommodation, improve hospitality and launch new services for pilgrims.",""]],"8":[[1,"27","1","Family Planning Culture Promotion","Families will also be encouraged to adopt a planning culture, to plan carefully for their future and the futures of their children.",""],[1,"28","1","Social Welfare System Modernization Reform","We will continue modernizing our social welfare system to make it more efficient, empowering and just.",""],[1,"28","1","Targeted Subsidy Redirection Policy","Subsidies for fuel, food, water and electricity will be better utilized by redirecting them towards those in need.",""],[1,"28","1","Tailored Vulnerable Citizen Support Programme","We will provide our most vulnerable citizens with tailored care and support.",""],[1,"71","4","Personal Financial Planning Tools Provision","We will promote greater financial independence by providing planning tools such as mortgages, savings portfolios, and retirement options.",""]],"9":[[1,"22","1","Drug Abuse Prevention and Control Efforts","supporting ongoing efforts to fight drugs abuse",""],[1,"22","1","Traffic Safety Improvement Measures","adopting further measures to ensure traffic safety, reduce traffic accidents and minimize their tragic consequences",""],[1,"22","1","Essential Urban Services Provision","we will continue to ensure high quality services such as water, electricity, public transport and roads are properly provided",""],[1,"22","1","Open and Landscaped Areas Development","Open and landscaped areas will also be developed further, to meet the recreational needs of individuals and families",""]],"10":[[1,"22","3","Waste Management Efficiency Improvement","We will seek to safeguard our environment by increasing the efficiency of waste management",""],[1,"22","3","Comprehensive Recycling Projects","establishing comprehensive recycling projects",""],[1,"22","3","Pollution Reduction Initiative","reducing all types of pollution",""],[1,"22","3","Desertification Control Programme","fighting desertification",""],[1,"22","3","Water Consumption Reduction Initiative","We will also promote the optimal use of our water resources by reducing consumption",""],[1,"22","3","Treated and Renewable Water Utilization","utilizing treated and renewable water",""],[1,"22","3","Coastal and Natural Area Protection and Rehabilitation","We will direct our efforts towards protecting and rehabilitating our beautiful beaches, natural reserves and islands, making them open to everyone.",""],[1,"22","3","Public-Private Environmental Financing Mechanism","We will seek the participation of the private sector and government funds in these efforts.",""]],"11":[[1,"64","5","Strategic Food Reserves Programme","We will continue to build safe and sufficient strategic food reserves, to better guard against emergencies.",""],[1,"64","5","Aquaculture Promotion Programme","Aquaculture will be promoted",""],[1,"64","5","Strategic Food Resource Partnerships","strategic partnerships with countries blessed with natural resources such as fertile soil and water reserves",""],[1,"64","5","Water Prioritization for Agriculture","the use of water in agriculture will be prioritized for those areas with natural and renewable water sources",""],[1,"64","5","Food Resource Waste Reduction Initiative","We will also continue to collaborate with consumers, food manufacturers and distributors to reduce any resource wastage.",""]],"12":[[1,"35","5","SME Entrepreneurship Support Programme","Therefore, we will strive to create suitable job opportunities for our citizens by supporting SME entrepreneurship",""],[1,"35","5","SME Authority","we have established the SME Authority",""],[1,"35","5","Business-Friendly SME Regulation","encouraging our young entrepreneurs with business-friendly regulations",""],[1,"35","5","SME Funding Access Mechanism","encouraging our young entrepreneurs with business-friendly regulations, easier access to funding",""],[1,"35","5","International SME Partnership Programme","encouraging our young entrepreneurs with business-friendly regulations, easier access to funding, international partnerships",""],[1,"35","5","SME Public Procurement Access Programme","a greater share of national procurement and government bids",""],[1,"35","5","Productive Family Digital Market Access","We will facilitate access to these channels",""],[1,"35","5","Productive Family Microfinance Facility","enable microfinance",""],[1,"35","5","Productive Family Capability-Building Initiative","motivate the non-profit sector to build the capabilities of our productive families",""],[1,"35","5","Productive Family Initiative Funding","fund their initiatives",""],[1,"40","2","SME Financing Access and Allocation Initiative","We will strive to facilitate enhanced access to funding and to encourage our financial institutions to allocate up to 20 percent of overall funding to SMEs by 2030.",""],[1,"40","2","SME Regulatory and Administrative Reform","The recently established SME Authority plans to review laws and regulations thoroughly, remove obstacles",""],[1,"40","2","Entrepreneurial Ideas and Product Market Access Support","enable youth and entrepreneurs to market their ideas and products",""],[1,"40","2","Business Incubator Establishment Programme","we will establish additional new business incubators",""],[1,"40","2","Specialized Entrepreneurial Training Institutions","we will establish additional new ... specialized training institutions",""],[1,"40","2","SME Venture Capital Fund Establishment","we will establish additional new ... venture capital funds",""],[1,"40","2","SME Marketing and Export Support Programme","We will also support SMEs in marketing and help export their products and services, by leveraging e-commerce and collaborating with international stakeholders.",""]],"13":[[1,"12","2","Business Environment Improvement Reform","improving the business environment",""],[1,"12","2","Government Services Privatization Programme","privatizing some government services",""],[1,"42","1","Government Services Privatization Reform","PRIVATIZE SOME GOVERNMENT SERVICES",""],[1,"44","1","Government Services Privatization Policy","PRIVATIZING OUR GOVERNMENT SERVICES",""],[1,"41","4","State-Owned Asset Privatization Programme","The ongoing privatization of state-owned assets, including leading companies, property and other assets, will bring in new and more diverse revenues for the Saudi government.",""],[1,"82","3","Privatization Program","THE PRIVATIZATION PROGRAM",""],[1,"82","4","Comprehensive Privatization Program","Our goal is to create a comprehensive privatization program.",""],[1,"44","2","New Investment Opportunities Initiative","we will open up new investment opportunities",""],[1,"44","2","Investment Facilitation Mechanism","facilitate investment",""],[1,"44","2","Innovation and Competition Promotion Policy","encourage innovation and competition",""],[1,"44","2","Private Sector Barrier Removal Reform","remove all obstacles preventing the private sector from playing a larger role in development",""],[1,"44","2","Investor-Focused Regulatory Reform","We will continue to improve and reform our regulations",""],[1,"44","3","Private Sector Investment Promotion Initiative","We will seek to increase private sector contribution by encouraging investments, both local and international, in healthcare, municipal services, housing, finance, energy and so forth.",""],[1,"49","4","Public-Private Partnership Development","We will further pursue public-private partnerships",""],[1,"82","6","Public-Private Partnership Development","We are identifying opportunities for partnering with the private sector",""],[1,"49","4","Business Regulation Review","We will coordinate with legislative authorities to review current regulations with the aim of improving the business environment",""],[1,"49","4","Contract Enforcement Improvement","enforcing contracts",""],[1,"49","4","Expedited Business Licensing Procedures","We will also facilitate and expedite licensing procedures based on our national economic priorities.",""],[1,"49","4","International Legal and Commercial Regulation Enforcement","We will apply international legal and commercial regulations strictly",""]],"14":[[1,"6","1","Public Investment Fund Expansion","We will transform the Public Investment Fund into the world’s largest sovereign wealth fund.",""],[1,"41","4","Investment Vehicle Sophistication Development","We will develop further the sophistication of our investment vehicles",""],[1,"41","4","Aramco Ownership Transfer to Public Investment Fund","transferring the ownership of Aramco to the Public Investment Fund",""],[1,"41","5","Sovereign Wealth Fund Management Efficiency Reform","We will increase the efficiency of the fund’s management and improve its return on investment, with the aim of diversifying our government resources and our economy.",""],[1,"41","5","Strategic Sector Investment and National Corporation Development","The Public Investment Fund will not compete with the private sector, but instead help unlock strategic sectors requiring intensive capital inputs.",""],[1,"64","1","Public Investment Fund Efficiency Reform","We will work to further improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the Public Investment Fund.",""],[1,"81","1","Public Investment Fund Restructuring Program","THE PUBLIC INVESTMENT FUND RESTRUCTURING PROGRAM",""],[1,"81","2","Sovereign Wealth Fund Investment Capability Expansion","we are now refining its investment capabilities and enabling the fund to manage a broader portfolio of current and new assets.",""],[1,"54","3","Public Investment Fund Headquarters Establishment","The district will be the headquarters of the Public Investment Fund, the largest sovereign wealth fund, which will contribute to creating an environment attractive to financial, investment and other corporations.",""]],"15":[[1,"42","3","Advanced Financial and Capital Market Development","All of this will require the formation of an advanced financial and capital market open to the world",""],[1,"42","3","Stock Market Investment Access Facilitation","We will continue facilitating access to investing and trading in the stock markets.",""],[1,"42","3","Private and State-Owned Enterprise Listing Facilitation","We will smooth the process of listing private Saudi companies and state-owned enterprises, including Aramco.",""],[1,"42","3","Capital Market Liquidity and Market Infrastructure Development","This will require deepening liquidity in our capital markets, fortifying the role of the debt market and paving the way for the derivatives market.",""],[1,"64","1","Budget Balancing and Revenue Diversification Policy","We shall prudently and efficiently balance our budget, as well as diversify and maximize our revenue sources.",""],[1,"64","1","Non-Oil Revenue and Economic Diversification Programme","Non-oil revenues will increase as logistics and trade flows increase, and as we grow a more diversified and balanced Saudi economy.",""],[1,"64","1","Oil Production and Revenue Management Programme","We will continue to manage oil production effectively to ensure a rewarding flow of oil revenue and reinvestment.",""],[1,"64","1","Government License and Service Fee Reform","We will revamp government license and service fees and develop the appropriate collection tools.",""],[1,"80","1","Fiscal Balance Program","THE FISCAL BALANCE PROGRAM",""],[1,"80","2","Non-Oil Revenue Diversification Measures","We plan to continue diversifying our non-oil revenues in the coming years, by introducing new measures.",""]],"16":[[1,"6","1","Aramco Industrial Transformation","we will transform Aramco from an oil producing company into a global industrial conglomerate",""],[1,"6","1","Domestic Military Manufacturing Programme","we plan to manufacture half of our military needs within the Kingdom",""],[1,"6","1","Military Equipment Modernization","we continue to give our army the best possible machinery and equipment",""],[1,"47","1","Localized Defense Industries Development","LOCALIZED DEFENSE INDUSTRIES",""],[1,"47","2","Military Equipment Spending Localization Programme","We have already begun developing less complex industries such as those providing spare parts, armored vehicles and basic ammunition.",""],[1,"47","2","Integrated National Defense Industry Network","We will build an integrated national network of services and supporting industries that will improve our self-sufficiency and strengthen our defense exports, both regionally and internationally.",""],[1,"47","2","Defense Industry Investment and Partnership Mechanism","Localization will be achieved through direct investments and strategic partnerships with leading companies in this sector.",""],[1,"47","2","Defense Industry Knowledge and Technology Transfer","These moves will transfer knowledge and technology, and build national expertise in the fields of manufacturing, maintenance, repair, research and development.",""],[1,"47","2","Defense Workforce Training and Industrial Complex Development","We will also train our employees and establish more specialized and integrated industrial complexes.",""],[1,"81","6","Saudi Aramco Strategic Transformation Program","THE SAUDI ARAMCO STRATEGIC TRANSFORMATION PROGRAM",""],[1,"81","7","Saudi Aramco Multi-Sector Transformation Programme","it has worked on a sweeping transformative program that will position it as a leader in more than one sector.",""]],"17":[[1,"43","2","Renewable Energy and Industrial Equipment Localization Programme","In the manufacturing sector, we will work towards localizing renewable energy and industrial equipment sectors.",""],[1,"43","3","Oil and Gas Sector Localization Policy","we will continue to localize the oil and gas sector.",""],[1,"43","3","Energy City Development Project","creating a new city dedicated to energy",""],[1,"43","3","National Gas Production Expansion","we will double our gas production",""],[1,"43","3","National Gas Distribution Network","construct a national gas distribution network",""],[1,"48","4","King Salman Renewable Energy Initiative","We will put this into practice with the forthcoming launch of the King Salman Renewable Energy Initiative.",""],[1,"48","4","Renewable Energy Value Chain Localization Programme","We will also seek to localize a significant portion of the renewable energy value chain in the Saudi economy, including research and development, and manufacturing, among other stages.",""],[1,"48","4","Renewable Energy Investment Regulatory Review","We will review the legal and regulatory framework that allows the private sector to buy and invest in the renewable energy sector.",""],[1,"48","4","Renewable Energy Public-Private Partnership Mechanism","To localize the industry and produce the necessary skill-sets, we will also encourage public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"48","4","Fuel Market Liberalization Reform","Finally, we will guarantee the competitiveness of renewable energy through the gradual liberalization of the fuels market.",""],[1,"50","4","Targeted Energy Subsidy Reform","We will also seek to set clear subsidy criteria based on the maturity of economic sectors, their ability to compete locally and internationally and their actual need for subsidies, without endangering promising and strategic sectors.",""],[1,"50","5","Energy Market Deregulation","DEREGULATE THE ENERGY MARKET TO MAKE IT MORE COMPETITIVE",""]],"18":[[1,"43","3","Mineral Resources Exploration Incentive Scheme","In mining, we will furnish incentives for and benefit from the exploration of the Kingdom’s mineral resources.",""],[1,"48","2","Mining Exploration Intensification","intensifying exploration",""],[1,"48","2","National Mineral Resources Database","building a comprehensive database of the Kingdom’s resources",""],[1,"48","2","Mining Extraction Licensing Review","reviewing the licensing procedures for extraction",""],[1,"48","2","Mining Sector Infrastructure Investment","investing in infrastructure",""],[1,"48","2","Mining Sector Funding Methods","developing funding methods",""],[1,"48","2","Mining Sector Centers of Excellence","establishing centers of excellence",""],[1,"48","2","Strategic International Mining Partnerships","We will also form strategic international partnerships",""],[1,"48","2","National Mining Company Competitiveness Programme","raise the competitiveness and productivity of our national companies",""]],"19":[[1,"43","2","International Tourism Attractions Development Programme","We will create attractions that are of the highest international standards",""],[1,"43","2","Visitor Visa Issuance Improvement Reform","improve visa issuance procedures for visitors",""],[1,"49","4","Strategic Government Land Allocation","We will allocate prime areas within cities for educational institutions, retail and entertainment centers, large areas along our coasts will be dedicated to tourist projects and appropriate lands will be allocated for industrial projects.",""],[1,"49","5","Rehabilitation Programme for Economic Cities","REHABILITATING ECONOMIC CITIES",""],[1,"49","6","Jizan Economic City Restructuring","We have worked in cooperation with Aramco to restructure Jizan Economic City.",""],[1,"49","6","Economic Cities Revitalization and Facilities Transfer","We will strive to salvage other economic cities, especially those with comparative advantages.",""],[1,"50","2","Special Economic Zones Development Programme","then establish special zones, such as logistic, tourist, industrial and financial ones.",""],[1,"50","2","Special Commercial Regulations for Investment Zones","Special commercial regulations to boost investment possibilities and diversify government revenues will be applied to these zones.",""],[1,"50","5","Economic Cities Restructuring","RESTRUCTURE OUR ECONOMIC CITIES",""],[1,"50","5","Special Economic Zones Creation","CREATE SPECIAL ZONES",""],[1,"54","2","King Abdullah Financial District Special Zone Strategy","We will seek to transform the district into a special zone that has competitive regulations and procedures, with visa exemptions, and directly connected to the King Khaled International Airport.",""],[1,"54","3","Built-Up Area Repurposing and Real Estate Mix Reform","We will also seek to repurpose some of the built-up areas and change the real estate mix, increasing the allocation for residential accommodation, services and hospitality areas.",""],[1,"54","3","Integrated Living and Working Environment Development","We will seek to build and create an integrated and attractive living and working environment.",""],[1,"56","2","Retail Investment Attraction Initiative","This will be achieved by attracting both regional and international retail investors",""],[1,"56","2","Foreign Ownership and Investment Liberalization Reform","by easing restrictions on ownership and foreign investment",""],[1,"56","2","Local and Regional Goods Flow Facilitation","we will facilitate local and regional flow of goods",""],[1,"56","2","Retail Sector Regulatory Development","develop necessary sectoral regulations",""],[1,"56","2","Small Retail Enterprise Financing Mechanism","We will also increase financing of small retail enterprises to stimulate their growth and development.",""]],"20":[[1,"43","2","Digital Economy Investment and Leadership Programme","In technology, we will increase our investments in, and lead, the digital economy.",""],[1,"56","4","High-Speed Broadband Infrastructure Development","We will partner with the private sector to develop the telecommunications and information technology infrastructure, especially high-speed broadband, expanding its coverage and capacity within and around cities and improving its quality.",""],[1,"56","4","Broadband-Enabling Building Standards","We will also develop building standards to facilitate the extension of broadband networks.",""],[1,"56","4","National Digital Transformation Governance Council","We will strengthen the governance of digital transformation through a national council.",""],[1,"56","4","Telecommunications Regulation Improvement","We will also improve our regulations",""],[1,"56","4","Telecom Operator Partnership Mechanism","We will also improve our regulations and establish an effective partnership with telecom operators to better develop this critical infrastructure.",""],[1,"56","4","Local Telecommunications and IT Investment Support","We will also support local investments in the telecommunications and information technology sectors.",""]],"21":[[1,"6","1","Global Expansion of Major Corporations","We will encourage our major corporations to expand across borders and take their rightful place in global markets.",""],[1,"12","2","Global Talent and Investment Attraction Initiative","attracting the finest talent and the best investments globally",""],[1,"42","2","Long-Term International Knowledge and Trade Partnerships","we plan to enter long-term partnerships with neighboring and friendly countries for knowledge transfer and trade.",""],[1,"42","2","International Investment and Emerging Technology Participation","Our Vision is to maximize our investment capabilities by participating in large international companies and emerging technologies from around the world.",""],[1,"57","1","Strategic Partnership Development","AGREE NEW STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIPS",""],[1,"57","4","Integrated Infrastructure Completion and Connectivity Partnerships","We plan to work with the private sector and enter into a new series of international partnerships to complete, improve and link our infrastructure internally and across borders.",""],[1,"57","4","Transport Capacity Utilisation and Trade Route Expansion","Air, maritime, and other transport operators will be encouraged to make the most of their capacity: achieving durable links between existing trade hubs, as well as opening new trade routes.",""],[1,"57","6","New International Business Partnerships","We will seek to establish new business partnerships",""],[1,"57","6","Cross-Border Movement Facilitation","facilitate a smoother flow of goods, people and capital",""],[1,"57","6","GCC Economic Integration and Interconnectivity","fortify and extend our interconnectivity and economic integration with other Gulf Cooperation Council countries",""],[1,"57","6","GCC Common Market Implementation","complete the process of implementing the GCC common market",""],[1,"57","6","GCC Customs and Policy Harmonization","unifying customs, economic and legal policies",""],[1,"57","6","Shared GCC Road and Railway Networks","constructing shared road and railway networks",""],[1,"57","6","Regional Logistics Services Expansion","through enhanced logistics services",""],[1,"58","1","Cross-Border Transport Infrastructure Projects","new cross-border infrastructure projects, including land transport projects with Africa through Egypt.",""],[1,"58","2","Saudi Company Export Support Initiative","HELP SAUDI COMPANIES TO INCREASE EXPORTS OF THEIR PRODUCTS.",""],[1,"58","2","Industrialization and Export Catalyzation Initiative","WE WILL LEVERAGE THE CLOSE PROXIMITY OF ENERGY SOURCES AND OUR DISTINCTIVE LOGISTICAL OFFER TO STIMULATE A NEW PHASE OF INDUSTRIALIZATION AND TO CATALYZE EXPORTS AND RE-EXPORTS",""],[1,"58","4","Major National Company Global Promotion Programme","Initially, our priority will be to fully support major national companies, which have already gained a leading market share, by promoting their products and services regionally and globally, especially in the fields of oil, petrochemicals, banking, telecommunications, food, health care, and retail.",""],[1,"58","4","Saudi Company Growth and Global Leadership Support","We will also seek to support Saudi companies with promising growth opportunities so they develop into new regional and global leaders.",""],[1,"58","4","National Industry Export Promotion Support","Finally, we will fully support our national industries, assisting them to market themselves abroad and to export their products.",""],[1,"82","2","Strategic Economic Partnerships and Export Hub Initiative","We are working with our economic partners around the world to build new strategic partnerships for the twenty-first century, in harmony with our national Vision, so that we can be a trade hub connecting three continents and enhance our exports.",""],[1,"49","4","Transport and Customs Facilitation","We will strive to facilitate the movement of people and goods, and to simplify customs procedures at our ports.",""]],"22":[[1,"6","1","Digital Government Services Expansion","We will expand the variety of digital services to reduce delays and cut tedious bureaucracy.",""],[1,"6","2","World-Class Government Services Reform","providing world-class government services which effectively and efficiently meet the needs of our citizens",""],[1,"64","3","Online Government Services Expansion","Transparency will be boosted and delays reduced by expanding online services and improving their governance standards.",""],[1,"70","3","Expansion of Online Government Services","We will expand the scope of current online services further to include areas such as geographic information, health care and education.",""],[1,"70","3","Online Service Quality Improvement","Quality will be improved by streamlining processes, and diversifying communication channels.",""],[1,"70","3","Government Cloud and Data Systems Adoption","We will also support the wider use of online applications in government agencies, such as cloud applications, data sharing platforms and HR management systems.",""],[1,"70","3","Online Services Governance Strengthening","Finally, we will strengthen the governance of online services within the government itself.",""],[1,"64","6","Government Service Quality Improvement","We will encourage government agencies to improve the quality of their services and to meet the needs of every citizen.",""]],"23":[[1,"6","1","Government Transparency and Accountability Reform","We will immediately adopt wide-ranging transparency and accountability reforms",""],[1,"6","1","Government Agency Performance Accountability Mechanism","through the body set up to measure the performance of government agencies, hold them accountable for any shortcomings",""],[1,"63","3","Government Performance Tracking Mechanism","TO TRACKING BOTH THEIR OWN PERFORMANCE AND THAT OF THE GOVERNMENT OVERALL",""],[1,"64","2","Government Monitoring Units Development and Support","We will continue to develop monitoring units and help them with recruitment, budgets and other organizational support.",""],[1,"64","3","International Administrative Standards Adoption","We will adopt leading international standards and administrative practices.",""],[1,"64","3","Accountability Standards Framework","We will set and uphold high standards of accountability.",""],[1,"64","3","Public Performance Transparency Mechanism","Our goals, plan and performance indicators will be published so that progress and delivery can be publicly monitored.",""],[1,"80","8","Government Performance Measurement and Evaluation System","We adopted the principle of performance measurement, and made sure it is properly used in our evaluation of all government agencies, their programs, initiatives and executives.",""],[1,"80","8","Center for Performance Management of Government Agencies","We established the Center for Performance Management of Government Agencies to institutionalize these efforts for the long-term",""],[1,"80","8","Government Performance Dashboards","built performance dashboards to promote accountability and transparency.",""],[1,"83","1","Vision Performance Review and Assessment Mechanism","WE WILL CONTINUOUSLY REVIEW AND ASSESS OUR PERFORMANCE IN ACHIEVING THIS VISION",""],[1,"82","6","Performance-Tracked Initiative Design","We are detailing specific initiatives that have clear performance indicators.",""]],"24":[[1,"63","3","Efficient and Effective Public Finance Management","WE ARE COMMITTED TO MANAGING OUR FINANCES EFFICIENTLY AND EFFECTIVELY",""],[1,"63","3","Agile Public Organization Reform","TO CREATING AGILE PUBLIC ORGANIZATIONS",""],[1,"64","1","Public Spending Efficiency and Control Programme","We will seek to eliminate waste and continue to make spending more efficient through stricter spending controls.",""],[1,"64","1","Public Project Review and Performance Control","We have reviewed all our existing and approved projects to ensure that they will have a sufficiently positive impact on the nation and our economy.",""],[1,"70","1","QAWAM Spending Efficiency Programme","“QAWAM”: INCREASING SPENDING EFFICIENCY",""],[1,"70","2","Qawam Public Spending Efficiency Programme","Through this program, we will comprehensively review financial regulations in all government agencies.",""],[1,"80","2","Capital Expenditure Review and Approval Mechanism","We began examining our existing capital expenditures, their approval mechanism and their measureable economic impact.",""],[1,"80","2","Expenditure Regulation Review Committees and Departments","We have formed committees and introduced new departments tasked with reviewing relevant regulations and taking the necessary action on the expenditures.",""],[1,"80","3","Project Management Program","THE PROJECT MANAGEMENT PROGRAM",""],[1,"80","4","Government Project Management Approach","we adopted an effective approach to project management",""],[1,"80","4","Government Project Management Offices","established expert project management offices (PMOs) in the Council of Economic and Development Affairs and many other government agencies",""],[1,"80","4","Central Delivery Unit","We also set up a central Delivery Unit.",""]],"25":[[1,"64","1","Civil Service Management and Shared Services Reform","We will also plan for better management of our talented civil service, and provide shared services within our government according to best practices.",""],[1,"64","2","Government Structure and Procedure Review","We will carefully examine our government structures and procedures, roles, responsibilities and capabilities.",""],[1,"68","2","Government Employee Distance Learning Programme","by 2020, we aim to have trained, through distance learning, 500,000 government employees.",""],[1,"68","2","Government Human Capital Development Standards","All ministries and government institutions will be required to adopt best practices in human capital development.",""],[1,"68","2","Merit-Based Government Recruitment and Talent Development","We will continue to hire individuals according to merit and work towards building a broad talent base, so they may become leaders of the future.",""],[1,"68","2","Government Human Capital Development Centers of Excellence","The King Salman Program for Human Capital Development will establish HR centers of excellence in every government agency, and provide training.",""],[1,"68","2","Government Employee Performance Management Standards","by implementing proper performance management standards",""],[1,"68","2","Continuous Professional Development for Government Employees","providing continuous training for professional development",""],[1,"68","2","Government Knowledge-Sharing Mechanism","sharing knowledge",""],[1,"68","2","Future Leadership Identification and Empowerment Policies","We will develop targeted policies to identify and empower future leaders",""],[1,"68","2","Equal Opportunity and Excellence Reward System","will furnish a stimulating environment that provides equal opportunities and rewards for excellence.",""],[1,"68","4","Government Shared Services Reform","We are working towards shared services across our government agencies.",""],[1,"78","2","Government Restructuring Program","THE GOVERNMENT RESTRUCTURING PROGRAM",""],[1,"78","3","Government Institutional Restructuring and Council Establishment","We have already started moving along this path by eliminating supreme councils and establishing the Council of Political and Security Affairs and the Council of Economic and Development Affairs.",""],[1,"82","8","Government Agency Restructuring and Streamlining","We will work on restructuring our government agencies continuously and with flexibility.",""],[1,"82","8","Strategic Government Management Office","Under the Council of Economic and Development Affairs, we will establish a strategic management office to focus on coordinating all government programs and ensuring their careful alignment with the national Vision.",""],[1,"82","8","Royal Court Decision Support Center","We will also establish a Decision Support Center at the Royal Court to support decision-making through analytical and evidence-based information and reports.",""],[1,"81","4","Human Talent Development and Civil Service Efficiency Programme","Because human capital is a crucial factor in the success of any substantial project, we aim to launch a thorough program for nurturing our human talent. This program will measure, assess and analyze the efficiency of our civil service. It will also support our government agencies with staff, studies, consultations, and strategic partnerships related to human capital.",""]],"26":[[1,"12","2","Vision-Aligned Future Projects Mechanism","all future projects are aligned to its content",""],[1,"12","2","Executive and Crucial Programme Portfolio","We will now launch a first portfolio of crucial programs with the aim to achieve our goals and honor our commitments.",""],[1,"57","4","Laws and Regulations Implementation Improvement","We will improve and implement existing laws and regulations.",""],[1,"64","6","Online Citizen Engagement Mechanisms","We shall facilitate interactive, online and smart engagement methods and ways to listen to citizens’ views.",""],[1,"80","5","Regulations Review Program","THE REGULATIONS REVIEW PROGRAM",""],[1,"80","6","Comprehensive Legal and Regulatory Review","We will continue to review all laws to ensure they are in line with the Kingdom’s priorities.",""],[1,"81","5","Executive Programs Launch Initiative","WE ARE PREPARING TO LAUNCH A GROUP OF EXECUTIVE PROGRAMS THAT WILL HAVE A SIGNIFICANT IMPACT ON IMPLEMENTATION.",""],[1,"82","6","Government Agency Implementation Workshops","our government agencies have been working through numerous workshops to examine their role in implementing the initiatives necessary for delivering on national priorities.",""],[1,"82","6","Innovative Administrative and Funding Approaches","innovative administrative and funding approaches",""]],"27":[[1,"71","4","Non-Profit Sector Regulatory Framework","We will set up a regulatory framework that empowers the non-profit sector.",""],[1,"76","2","Non-Profit Sector Regulatory Framework","The recently published regulations on non-profit organizations and on the General Authority for Endowments will help the non-profit sector become more institutionalized, formalized and more efficient.",""],[1,"72","5","Social and Compassionate Work Organization Reform","In the future, we will formalize and strengthen the organization of our social and compassionate work so that our efforts have the maximum results and impact.",""],[1,"72","5","Non-Profit Sector Regulatory and Endowment Reform","We will review our regulations to encourage endowments to sustainably fund the sector and to encourage corporations and high net worth families to establish non-profit organizations.",""],[1,"72","5","Impact-Based Government Support for Non-Profit Programs","Government support will be directed to the programs with highest social impact",""],[1,"72","5","Non-Profit Workforce Training and Volunteering Programme","we will support training workers to encourage volunteering and careers in the non-profit sector.",""],[1,"72","5","Non-Profit Talent and Knowledge Management Initiative","Enabling non-profit organizations to attract the best talents in order to ensure best management practices and the transfer of knowledge, which will strengthen these institutions over the long-term.",""],[1,"76","2","High-Impact Non-Profit Projects and Programmes","We will accelerate this shift further by supporting projects and programs with high social impact",""],[1,"76","2","Non-Profit Organization Establishment Facilitation","facilitating the establishment of non-profit organizations by high net worth families",""],[1,"76","2","Government and Non-Profit Sector Collaboration Mechanism","We will support this growth by creating a supportive and cooperate environment in which the sector’s institutions and government agencies can collaborate.",""],[1,"76","3","Non-Profit Governance Standards Initiative","encourage the non-profit sector to apply proper governance standards",""],[1,"76","3","Non-Profit Staff Training Programme","facilitate high quality training to staff",""],[1,"76","3","Non-Profit Volunteering and Careers Promotion","promote a culture of volunteering and full-time careers in the sector",""]]}});